<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτωλ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>erroneous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτωλότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1109a33
				</span></i>
			; <i>erring,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν πᾶσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.25c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of bad character,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Ir.</u>
					p.73
				</span></i>
			 W.: c. gen., <i>sinning against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					547.31
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Telmessus</span>):—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτωλὴ γέρων,</span> barbarism in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1111
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					24D.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμαρτωλός, ὁ,</span>
			<i>sinner,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				13.13
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				18.13
			</span></i>, al.</div>
